-- ccc2-official-documents.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II, ss 56.1 to 58 ("Official Documents"): identity documents, forged passports,
-- fraudulent use of a certificate of citizenship. Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the
-- Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words) / NOTHING (not covered): see the header of ccc2-treason.l4 and NOTES.md.

§ `Section 57(5) -- passport (the Canadian Passport Order, outside the sources)`

-- "In this section, passport has the same meaning as in section 2 of the Canadian Passport Order." The Order is not among the sources: its answer is a seam input.
-- src:1006 | Definition of passport
-- src:1007 | (5) In this section, passport has the same meaning as in section 2 of the Canadian Passport Order.
@ref Criminal Code s 57(5) (definition of passport) (src:1006-1007)
GIVEN `it is a passport as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Passport Order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57(5) the document is a passport` MEANS
    CONSIDER `it is a passport as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Passport Order`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "passport has the same meaning as in section 2 of the Canadian Passport Order" (the definition is handed to the Order, and the Order says no)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Canadian Passport Order is not among the sources

§ `Section 56.1 -- Identity documents`

-- Subsection (3): "identity document means a Social Insurance Number card, a driver's licence, a health insurance card, a birth certificate, a death certificate, a passport as defined in subsection 57(5),
-- a document that simplifies the process of entry into Canada, a certificate of citizenship, a document indicating immigration status in Canada, a certificate of Indian status or an employee identity card
-- that bears the employee's photograph and signature, or any similar document, issued or purported to be issued by a department or agency of the federal government or of a provincial or foreign government."
-- A "means" definition: a document of none of the kinds, or not issued or purported to be issued by such a department or agency, is not an identity document (JUST FALSE).
-- Whether a document is "similar" is an open-textured judgment taken as a plain input (the kind `a document similar to one of those`).
-- src:981 | Definition of identity document
-- src:982 | (3) For the purposes of this section, identity document means a Social Insurance Number card, a driver’s licence, a health insurance card, a birth certificate, a death certificate, a passport as defined in subsection 57(5), a document that simplifies the process of entry into Canada, a certificate of citizenship, a document indicating immigration status in Canada, a certificate of Indian status or an employee identity card that bears the employee’s photograph and signature, or any similar document, issued or purported to be issued by a department or agency of the federal government or of a provincial or foreign government.
@ref Criminal Code s 56.1(3) (definition of identity document) (src:981-982)
DECLARE `s 56.1(3) kind of document` IS ONE OF
    `s 56.1(3) a Social Insurance Number card`
    `s 56.1(3) a driver's licence`
    `s 56.1(3) a health insurance card`
    `s 56.1(3) a birth certificate`
    `s 56.1(3) a death certificate`
    `s 56.1(3) a passport as defined in subsection 57(5)`
    `s 56.1(3) a document that simplifies the process of entry into Canada`
    `s 56.1(3) a certificate of citizenship`
    `s 56.1(3) a document indicating immigration status in Canada`
    `s 56.1(3) a certificate of Indian status`
    `s 56.1(3) an employee identity card that bears the employee's photograph and signature`
    `s 56.1(3) a document similar to one of those`
    `s 56.1(3) a document of none of those kinds`

@ref Criminal Code s 56.1(3) (definition of identity document) (src:981-982)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 56.1(3) kind of document`
      `it is issued or purported to be issued by a department or agency of the federal government or of a provincial or foreign government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 57(5) the document is a passport: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56.1(3) the document is an identity document` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is issued or purported to be issued by a department or agency of the federal government or of a provincial or foreign government` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "identity document means ... issued or purported to be issued by a department or agency of the federal government or of a provincial or foreign government"
        IF kind EQUALS `s 56.1(3) a document of none of those kinds` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "identity document means a Social Insurance Number card, a driver's licence"
        IF kind EQUALS `s 56.1(3) a passport as defined in subsection 57(5)` THEN `s 57(5) the document is a passport: the answer`   -- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING as section 57(5) answers
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Subsection (2): "For greater certainty, subsection (1) does not prohibit an act that is carried out (a) in good faith, in the ordinary course of the person's business or employment or in the
-- exercise of the duties of their office; (b) for genealogical purposes; (c) with the consent of the person to whom the identity document relates or of a person authorized to consent on behalf of
-- the person to whom the document relates, or of the entity that issued the identity document; or (d) for a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice." A flat negative (JUST FALSE).
-- src:975 | For greater certainty
-- src:976 | (2) For greater certainty, subsection (1) does not prohibit an act that is carried out
-- src:977 | (a) in good faith, in the ordinary course of the person’s business or employment or in the exercise of the duties of their office;
-- src:978 | (b) for genealogical purposes;
-- src:979 | (c) with the consent of the person to whom the identity document relates or of a person authorized to consent on behalf of the person to whom the document relates, or of the entity that issued the identity document; or
-- src:980 | (d) for a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice.
@ref Criminal Code s 56.1(2) (for greater certainty) (src:975-980)
GIVEN `the act is carried out in good faith, in the ordinary course of the person's business or employment or in the exercise of the duties of their office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is carried out for genealogical purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is carried out with the consent of the person to whom the identity document relates, of a person authorized to consent on their behalf, or of the entity that issued the identity document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is carried out for a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56.1(2) subsection 56.1(1) prohibits the act` MEANS
    IF `the act is carried out in good faith, in the ordinary course of the person's business or employment or in the exercise of the duties of their office`
        OR `the act is carried out for genealogical purposes`
        OR `the act is carried out with the consent of the person to whom the identity document relates, of a person authorized to consent on their behalf, or of the entity that issued the identity document`
        OR `the act is carried out for a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (1) does not prohibit an act that is carried out"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says what is not prohibited, not what is

-- Subsection (1): "Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, procures to be made, possesses, transfers, sells or offers for sale an identity document that relates or purports
-- to relate, in whole or in part, to another person."
-- src:973 | Identity documents
-- src:974 | 56.1 (1) Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, procures to be made, possesses, transfers, sells or offers for sale an identity document that relates or purports to relate, in whole or in part, to another person.
@ref Criminal Code s 56.1(1) (identity documents) (src:973-974)
DECLARE `s 56.1(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 56.1(1) procures to be made an identity document`
    `s 56.1(1) possesses an identity document`
    `s 56.1(1) transfers an identity document`
    `s 56.1(1) sells an identity document`
    `s 56.1(1) offers for sale an identity document`
    `s 56.1(1) an act that is none of those`

@ref Criminal Code s 56.1(1) (identity documents) (src:973-974)
GIVEN act IS A `s 56.1(1) act`
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 56.1(3) the document is an identity document: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document relates or purports to relate, in whole or in part, to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is carried out in good faith, in the ordinary course of the person's business or employment or in the exercise of the duties of their office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is carried out for genealogical purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is carried out with the consent of the person to whom the identity document relates, of a person authorized to consent on their behalf, or of the entity that issued the identity document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is carried out for a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56.1(1) the person commits the identity document offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 56.1(2) subsection 56.1(1) prohibits the act` `the act is carried out in good faith, in the ordinary course of the person's business or employment or in the exercise of the duties of their office` `the act is carried out for genealogical purposes` `the act is carried out with the consent of the person to whom the identity document relates, of a person authorized to consent on their behalf, or of the entity that issued the identity document` `the act is carried out for a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For greater certainty, subsection (1) does not prohibit an act that is carried out" (subsection (2))
        IF act EQUALS `s 56.1(1) an act that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "procures to be made, possesses, transfers, sells or offers for sale"
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        IF `s 56.1(3) the document is an identity document: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "identity document means" (subsection (3))
        IF `s 56.1(3) the document is an identity document: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the document relates or purports to relate, in whole or in part, to another person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an identity document that relates or purports to relate, in whole or in part, to another person"

-- src:983 | Punishment
-- src:984 | (4) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:985 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:986 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 56.1(4) (punishment) (src:983-986)
`s 56.1(4) the class of the offence under subsection 56.1(1)` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 56.1(4) (punishment) (src:983-986)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 56.1(4) the punishment for an offence under subsection 56.1(1)` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 57 -- Forgery of or uttering forged passport`

-- Subsection (1): "Every one who, while in or out of Canada, (a) forges a passport, or (b) knowing that a passport is forged (i) uses, deals with or acts on it, or (ii) causes or attempts to cause any person to use,
-- deal with or act on it, as if the passport were genuine, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years." "While in or out of Canada" sets no limit of place.
-- src:987 | Forgery of or uttering forged passport
-- src:988 | 57 (1) Every one who, while in or out of Canada,
-- src:989 | (a) forges a passport, or
-- src:990 | (b) knowing that a passport is forged
-- src:991 | (i) uses, deals with or acts on it, or
-- src:992 | (ii) causes or attempts to cause any person to use, deal with or act on it, as if the passport were genuine,
-- src:993 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 57(1) (forgery of or uttering forged passport) (src:987-993)
DECLARE `s 57(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 57(1)(a) forges a passport`
    `s 57(1)(b)(i) knowing that a passport is forged, uses, deals with or acts on it as if it were genuine`
    `s 57(1)(b)(ii) knowing that a passport is forged, causes or attempts to cause a person to use, deal with or act on it as if it were genuine`
    `s 57(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) and (b)`

@ref Criminal Code s 57(1) (forgery of or uttering forged passport) (src:987-993)
GIVEN act IS A `s 57(1) act`
      `s 57(5) the document is a passport: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the passport is forged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57(1) the person commits forgery of or uttering a forged passport` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 57(5) the document is a passport: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "passport has the same meaning as in section 2 of the Canadian Passport Order" (subsection (5))
        IF act EQUALS `s 57(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) and (b)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every one who, while in or out of Canada, (a) forges a passport, or (b) knowing that a passport is forged"
        IF `s 57(5) the document is a passport: the answer` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Canadian Passport Order is not among the sources
        IF act EQUALS `s 57(1)(a) forges a passport` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person knows that the passport is forged` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "knowing that a passport is forged"

@ref Criminal Code s 57(1) (punishment) (src:987-993)
`s 57(1) the class of the offence under subsection 57(1)` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 57(1) (punishment) (src:987-993)
`s 57(1) the punishment for an offence under subsection 57(1)` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- Subsection (2): "Every one who, while in or out of Canada, for the purpose of procuring a passport for himself or any other person or for the purpose of procuring any material alteration or addition to any
-- such passport, makes a written or an oral statement that he knows is false or misleading (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction."
-- src:994 | False statement in relation to passport
-- src:995 | (2) Every one who, while in or out of Canada, for the purpose of procuring a passport for himself or any other person or for the purpose of procuring any material alteration or addition to any such passport, makes a written or an oral statement that he knows is false or misleading
-- src:996 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- src:997 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 57(2) (false statement in relation to passport) (src:994-997)
DECLARE `s 57(2) purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 57(2) the purpose of procuring a passport for himself or any other person`
    `s 57(2) the purpose of procuring any material alteration or addition to any such passport`
    `s 57(2) another purpose`

@ref Criminal Code s 57(2) (false statement in relation to passport) (src:994-997)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 57(2) purpose`
      `the person makes a written or an oral statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the statement is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57(2) the person makes a false statement in relation to a passport` MEANS
    IF purpose EQUALS `s 57(2) another purpose` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of procuring a passport ... or for the purpose of procuring any material alteration or addition to any such passport"
    ELSE IF `the person makes a written or an oral statement` AND `the person knows the statement is false or misleading`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "makes a written or an oral statement that he knows is false or misleading"

@ref Criminal Code s 57(2) (punishment) (src:994-997)
`s 57(2) the class of the offence under subsection 57(2)` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 57(2) (punishment) (src:994-997)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 57(2) the punishment for an offence under subsection 57(2)` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- Subsection (3): "Every person who, without lawful excuse, has in their possession a forged passport or a passport in respect of which an offence under subsection (2) has been committed is guilty of
-- (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction."
