-- src:999 | (3) Every person who, without lawful excuse, has in their possession a forged passport or a passport in respect of which an offence under subsection (2) has been committed is guilty of
-- src:1000 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:1001 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 57(3) (possession of forged, etc., passport) (src:998-1001)
GIVEN `the person has the passport in their possession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 57(5) the document is a passport: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the passport is forged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an offence under subsection 57(2) has been committed in respect of the passport` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57(3) the person possesses a forged passport` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 57(5) the document is a passport: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "passport has the same meaning as in section 2 of the Canadian Passport Order" (subsection (5))
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        IF `the person has the passport in their possession` AND `s 57(5) the document is a passport: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`the passport is forged` OR `an offence under subsection 57(2) has been committed in respect of the passport`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "has in their possession a forged passport or a passport in respect of which an offence under subsection (2) has been committed"

@ref Criminal Code s 57(3) (punishment) (src:998-1001)
`s 57(3) the class of the offence under subsection 57(3)` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 57(3) (punishment) (src:998-1001)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 57(3) the punishment for an offence under subsection 57(3)` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- Subsection (4): "For the purposes of proceedings under this section, (a) the place where a passport was forged is not material; and (b) the definition false document in section 321, and section 366,
-- apply with such modifications as the circumstances require." (a) is a flat negative (JUST FALSE for "material"); (b) is a rule of reading whose modifications the text does not state (fork F7).
