    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of proceedings under this section"

-- Subsection (6): "Where a person is alleged to have committed, while out of Canada, an offence under this section, proceedings in respect of that offence may, whether or not that person is in Canada,
-- be commenced in any territorial division in Canada and the accused may be tried and punished in respect of that offence in the same manner as if the offence had been committed in that territorial division."
-- A "may" function whose gate is "where": ruling (b) of the periods ruling (the gate failing answers JUST FALSE) is followed and the group is listed for a lawyer (fork F8, marginal readings).
