-- src:1009 | (6) Where a person is alleged to have committed, while out of Canada, an offence under this section, proceedings in respect of that offence may, whether or not that person is in Canada, be commenced in any territorial division in Canada and the accused may be tried and punished in respect of that offence in the same manner as if the offence had been committed in that territorial division.
@ref Criminal Code s 57(6) (jurisdiction) (src:1008-1009)
GIVEN `the person is alleged to have committed the offence while out of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is one under section 57` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 territorial division: the place where the proceedings are to be commenced is one in Canada` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
