    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is alleged to have committed the offence while out of Canada` AND `the offence is one under section 57`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is alleged to have committed, while out of Canada, an offence under this section"
        IF `s 2 territorial division: the place where the proceedings are to be commenced is one in Canada` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any territorial division in Canada"

-- Subsection (7): "For greater certainty, the provisions of this Act relating to (a) requirements that an accused appear at and be present during proceedings, and (b) the exceptions to those requirements,
