§ `Section 58 -- Fraudulent use of certificate of citizenship`

-- Subsection (2): "In this section, certificate of citizenship and certificate of naturalization, respectively, mean a certificate of citizenship and a certificate of naturalization as defined by the
-- Citizenship Act." The Act is not among the sources: its answer is a seam input.
-- src:1019 | Definition of certificate of citizenship and certificate of naturalization
-- src:1020 | (2) In this section, certificate of citizenship and certificate of naturalization, respectively, mean a certificate of citizenship and a certificate of naturalization as defined by the Citizenship Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 58(2) (definition of certificate of citizenship and certificate of naturalization) (src:1019-1020)
GIVEN `it is a certificate of citizenship or a certificate of naturalization as defined by the Citizenship Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 58(2) the document is a certificate of citizenship or of naturalization` MEANS
    CONSIDER `it is a certificate of citizenship or a certificate of naturalization as defined by the Citizenship Act`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "certificate of citizenship and certificate of naturalization, respectively, mean a certificate of citizenship and a certificate of naturalization as defined by the Citizenship Act"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Citizenship Act is not among the sources

-- Subsection (1): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, while in or
-- outside Canada, (a) uses a certificate of citizenship or a certificate of naturalization for a fraudulent purpose, or (b) being a person to whom a certificate ... has been granted, knowingly parts with the
-- possession of that certificate with intent that it should be used for a fraudulent purpose."
-- src:1015 | Fraudulent use of certificate of citizenship
-- src:1016 | 58 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, while in or outside Canada,
-- src:1017 | (a) uses a certificate of citizenship or a certificate of naturalization for a fraudulent purpose, or
-- src:1018 | (b) being a person to whom a certificate of citizenship or a certificate of naturalization has been granted, knowingly parts with the possession of that certificate with intent that it should be used for a fraudulent purpose.
@ref Criminal Code s 58(1) (fraudulent use of certificate of citizenship) (src:1015-1018)
DECLARE `s 58(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 58(1)(a) uses a certificate of citizenship or a certificate of naturalization for a fraudulent purpose`
    `s 58(1)(b) being a person to whom the certificate has been granted, knowingly parts with its possession with intent that it should be used for a fraudulent purpose`
    `s 58(1) an act that is neither of those in paragraphs (a) and (b)`

@ref Criminal Code s 58(1) (fraudulent use of certificate of citizenship) (src:1015-1018)
GIVEN act IS A `s 58(1) act`
      `s 58(2) the document is a certificate of citizenship or of naturalization: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person to whom the certificate has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 58(1) the person fraudulently uses, or parts with, a certificate of citizenship or of naturalization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 58(2) the document is a certificate of citizenship or of naturalization: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "certificate of citizenship and certificate of naturalization, respectively, mean" (subsection (2))
        IF `s 58(2) the document is a certificate of citizenship or of naturalization: the answer` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Citizenship Act is not among the sources
        IF act EQUALS `s 58(1)(a) uses a certificate of citizenship or a certificate of naturalization for a fraudulent purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF act EQUALS `s 58(1)(b) being a person to whom the certificate has been granted, knowingly parts with its possession with intent that it should be used for a fraudulent purpose` AND `the person is a person to whom the certificate has been granted` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "being a person to whom a certificate of citizenship or a certificate of naturalization has been granted"

@ref Criminal Code s 58(1) (punishment) (src:1015-1018)
`s 58(1) the class of the offence under subsection 58(1)` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 58(1) (punishment) (src:1015-1018)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 58(1) the punishment for an offence under subsection 58(1)` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
